{"name":"Wood Avens","hex":"#fbeeac","fetched":"2026-10-13","looked":{"definitions":[{"term":"wood avens","whole":true,"parts":[{"part":"Noun","definitions":["Geum urbanum, herb bennet."]}],"link":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/wood_avens"}],"entries":[{"title":"Geum urbanum","blocks":[{"text":"Geum urbanum, also known as wood avens, herb Bennet, colewort, clove root and St. Benedict's herb, is a perennial plant in the rose family (Rosaceae), which grows in shady places in the temperate regions of Eurasia and North America."}],"image":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/b/b5/%28MHNT%29_Geum_urbanum_-_Habit.jpg/330px-%28MHNT%29_Geum_urbanum_-_Habit.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=api&utm_content=thumbnail","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Geum_urbanum","wikidata":"Q157407"},{"title":"Wood","blocks":[{"text":"Wood is a natural, lignocellulosic material derived primarily from the secondary xylem of trees and other woody plants, where it provides mechanical support and in the functional sapwood, conducts water and dissolved minerals. Being a natural material, it is characterized as an organic material – a natural composite of cellulosic fibers that are strong in tension and embedded in a matrix of lignin and hemicelluloses that resists compression."}],"image":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/4/4b/16_wood_samples.jpg/330px-16_wood_samples.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=api&utm_content=thumbnail","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Wood","wikidata":"Q287"}],"images":[{"srcset":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/9/9d/%28MHNT%29_Geum_urbanum_-_Buds_and_flower.jpg/330px-%28MHNT%29_Geum_urbanum_-_Buds_and_flower.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 1x, https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/9/9d/%28MHNT%29_Geum_urbanum_-_Buds_and_flower.jpg/960px-%28MHNT%29_Geum_urbanum_-_Buds_and_flower.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser